R"VG(
# sunlost3.vg (D-05): the myth of the sun walking away and the fires on the hills, every age's (the later ages' once `dark` >= 2);
# each sentence built of parts, each people keeping its own few of some (`people=K`). Also genre.omens' late log (the 16 KB a file).
@apart

genre.sunmyth (words=28..200)
  (age=prehistoric) {sm.p.wall} {sm.p.walker} {sm.p.way} {sm.p.fires} {sm.p.end}
  (age=prehistoric) {sm.p.wall} {sm.p.walker} {sm.p.way} {sm.p.fires} {sm.p.read}
  (tense=past age=medieval) {sm.m.head}\n{sm.tale}\n{sm.fires} {sm.m.close}
  (tense=past age=medieval) {sm.m.head} {sm.tale} {sm.after} {sm.m.close}
  (tense=past age>=industrial age<=modern medium=printed) {sm.i.head}\n{sm.tale}\n{sm.after} {sm.i.note}
  (tense=past age>=industrial age<=modern medium=cylinder|medium=drive|medium=crystal) {sm.v.head}\n{sm.tale} {sm.fires}\n{sm.v.end}
  (age>=industrial medium=disc|medium=reel) {sm.s.head}\n{sm.song}\n{sm.song.b}\n{sm.song}\n{sm.s.end}
  (tense=past age>=futuristic medium=crystal|medium=drive|medium=hum) {sm.f.head} {sm.tale}\n{sm.f.reflect}

# the myth: how the sun was, what came for it, how it walked away, where it is now

sm.tale
  {sm.begin} {sm.cause} {sm.away}
  {sm.begin} {sm.cause} {sm.away} {sm.now}
  {sm.cause} {sm.away} {sm.now}
sm.begin
  {sm.b.when} {sm.b.what}{sm.b.tail}.
  {sm.b.when} {sm.b.what}.
sm.b.when (people=3)
  In the first days,
  Long ago,
  Before the cold,
  When the {people} were few,
  In the time of the first {herd},
  When {mountain} was young,
sm.b.what (people=6)
  {god} set the sun on its road round the world
  the sun walked round our world once a year and never tired of it
  the sun was a {sm.being} who kept a road of its own
  the sun lived on the far side of {mountain} and walked over it every morning
  the sun and {god} walked the year's road together
  the sun came up over {mountain} every morning like a {sm.being} to its work
  the sun was as near as a fire, and the {crop} grew wherever it looked
  (faith=sky) {god.who} kept the sun on a cord, and the year was the cord's length
  (faith=ancestors) the first of the {people} gave the sun its road, and it kept to it
  (faith=land) the land and the sun were promised to each other
sm.b.tail
  , and it came home every year
  , and nobody thought it would stop
  , and the {herd} grew fat in its light
  , and the year was always the same length
sm.being (people=2)
  herder
  hunter
  old woman with a lamp
  great {beast}
  runner
  giant with a burning face
sm.cause
  {sm.c.lead} {sm.c.thing} {sm.c.did}{sm.c.tail}.
sm.c.lead
  But
  Then
  One year
  After many years,
sm.c.thing
  (sunway=wanderer) {sunway.thing}
  (sunway=wanderer) the wanderer, who walked a longer road,
  (sunway=intruder) a stranger star
  (sunway=intruder) a star with a bright face
  (sunway=intruder) {sunway.thing}
  (sunway=dark) something with no light
  (sunway=dark) a hungry thing
  (sunway=dark) a mouth in the sky
  (sunway=dance) the sun's sister
  (sunway=dance) {sunway.thing}
  (sunway=dance) the young sun
sm.c.did
  (sunway=wanderer) grew jealous of the sun's road
  (sunway=wanderer) came nearer every year
  (sunway=wanderer) leaned on our road with all its weight
  (sunway=wanderer) wanted the sun's road for itself
  (sunway=intruder) came out of the dark
  (sunway=intruder) courted the sun, nearer every night
  (sunway=intruder) called to the sun from the edge of the sky
  (sunway=intruder) grew brighter every year
  (sunway=dark) crept up behind the stars
  (sunway=dark) passed close, and could not be seen, only felt
  (sunway=dark) lay down across the road of the year
  (sunway=dark) came near without a sound
  (sunway=dance) danced wider every year
  (sunway=dance) pulled at our world as she danced
  (sunway=dance) let go of our world's hand
  (sunway=dance) spun us out of the ring
sm.c.tail
  (sunway=wanderer) , and the road bent toward it
  (sunway=wanderer) , and pulled the year out of shape
  (sunway=wanderer) , until the road broke
  (sunway=intruder) , and the sun went to meet it
  (sunway=intruder) , and the two suns quarrelled over us
  (sunway=intruder) , until nobody could say which sun was ours
  (sunway=dark) , and the stars bent away from it in fear
  (sunway=dark) , and the year fell into it
  (sunway=dark) , and the road came apart
  (sunway=dance) , and we went spinning into the dark
  (sunway=dance) , and the dance went on without us
  (sunway=dance) , and nobody caught us
sm.away
  {sm.a.sun}{sm.a.how}.
sm.a.sun (people=5)
  The sun walked away along the new road
  The sun went where it was pulled
  The sun turned its back on us
  The sun went slowly
  The sun followed it out past {mountain}
  The sun left without a word
  The sun went the way of {river}, and further
  The sun walked out of the year
sm.a.how (people=6)
  , a little smaller every year
  , and the summers went with it
  , and the warmth went after the summers
  , and did not look back
  , and the nights grew longer behind it
  , and the snow came after it, and then the air itself fell
  , and the {herd} called after it all one winter
  , and took the colours with it
sm.now
  (dark=3) {sm.n.now}{sm.n.tail}.
  (dark<=2) {sm.n.still}{sm.n.tail2}.
sm.n.now (people=4)
  Now it is a star among the stars
  Now it is no bigger than {star}
  Now you can hide it behind your thumb
  Now it is the brightest star in the sky, and no more
  Now it is a cold white point over {mountain}
  Now the {people} count it among the stars
sm.n.tail
  , and still walking
  , going the other way
  , if you know where to look
  , and the children do not believe it was ever the sun
sm.n.still
  It is walking still
  It has not gone far yet
  It can still be seen by day
sm.n.tail2
  , smaller every year
  ; it could still turn round
  , and the old ones watch it every morning
sm.fires
  {sm.f.lead} {sm.f.who} {sm.f.did}{sm.f.why}.
sm.f.lead
  So
  Every night of the first long winter,
  That winter,
  From then on,
sm.f.who (people=2)
  the {people}
  the old ones
  everyone who could walk
  the young of every village
sm.f.did (people=5)
  lit fires on every hill
  kept the {~hillfire} burning on {mountain}
  carried {fuel} up to the high places
  burned the {fuel}, then the {tree}, then the doors of their houses
  built the fires higher than the houses
  kept a fire on every roof of {city}
sm.f.why
  , so that the sun could see the way back
  , and sang {~sunsong} to it
  , until there was nothing left to burn
  , and in the morning the sun was still small
sm.after
  {sm.af.who} {sm.af.what}{sm.af.tail}.
sm.af.who
  The children say
  The old ones say
  (faith!=philosophy faith!=machine) The priests of {god} say
  Some of the {people} still say
sm.af.what (people=5)
  that the fires were too small
  that the sun will come back when it is tired of walking
  that the sun was taken because a fire was once let go out
  that the sun never looked back at all
  that it went to warm another people
  that it is still walking home, the long way round
  that {god} went with it
  (dark=3) that the fires on {mountain} should still be lit at {festival}
sm.af.tail
  , and they may be right
  , and nobody argues with them any more
  , though nobody believes it

# the old age: the story on a wall, a stone, a bone

sm.p.wall (formula)
  (medium=painted) {pre.wall.where}, a story in {pre.paint}.
  (medium=painted) A long picture along the wall, to be read walking.
  (medium=stone) Pecked into {pre.stone.where}: a story.
  (medium=bone) Cut round a {pre.bone}: a story that goes round it and does not end.
sm.p.walker
  {sm.p.sun} {sm.p.goes}.
sm.p.sun
  A figure with a round {colour.holy} face
  The sun, drawn as a figure with legs,
  A round {colour.holy} face on long legs
sm.p.goes
  walks away along it, over {mountain}, its back to the people
  walks off the edge of the stone, smaller in each picture than the one before
  stands large over {houses} at the start, and at the end it is a dot
sm.p.way
  (sunway=wanderer) Behind it, a bigger round thing with long arms, reaching for it.
  (sunway=wanderer) Above it, a second round face, larger, its mouth open.
  (sunway=intruder) Ahead of it, a star with rays, waiting with its arms open.
  (sunway=intruder) Beside it, a smaller sun with rays, holding its hand.
  (sunway=dark) Ahead of it, a black ring with nothing in it, and the stars drawn bent round the ring.
  (sunway=dark) A black ring is drawn across its road, and the road stops there.
  (sunway=dance) Two round faces dance with their hands joined; in the last picture one of them walks away.
  (sunway=dance) Two suns drawn turning round each other, and between them our world, falling out.
sm.p.fires
  {sm.p.fire1} {sm.p.fire2}.
sm.p.fire1
  On every hill a fire is drawn,
  Figures carry {fuel} up the hills in a line,
  The fires on the hills are drawn larger than the sun,
sm.p.fire2
  and figures beside the fires with their arms raised
  and the people by the fires are singing, their mouths open
  and the {herd} are drawn lying down by the fires
sm.p.read
  The ship reads it as a story told to children, and painted where they would see it.
  The ship takes the last figures for a prayer: the fires and the raised arms, again and again.
sm.p.end
  (medium=painted) {wall.state}
  (medium=stone) {stone.state}
  (medium=bone) The bone is black with handling.

# the medieval telling

sm.m.head (formula)
  This is how the old ones tell the going of the sun at {$home}.
  The tale of the sun's walking, as the priests of {holyplace} tell it.
  (medium=tablet) Set down from the telling of the old ones at {$home}.
  (medium=scroll|medium=codex) Here is written the oldest tale of the {people}, the tale of the sun that walked.
  (medium=stone) Cut by the door of {holyplace}, for those who cannot read it: the tale of the sun.
sm.m.close (formula)
  So the old ones tell it.
  (faith!=philosophy faith!=machine) Whether it is true, {god} knows.
  This is the tale as it was told to me; I have not changed it.
  (holy=highplace) The fire on the high place is kept for it still.

# the later ages: the story collected, a telling, a song, a reflection

sm.i.head (formula)
  From the old tales of {$home}, as the country people still tell them.
  The tale of the walking sun: an old story, set down by the society at {$seat}.
  (age=modern) The oldest story of the {people}, as it is told to children in {hall.below}.
sm.i.note
  The tale is older than the observatories, and it got the sun's road right.
  The collector adds that every hall below tells it a little differently.
  It is told now by the lamps, and the children ask what a hill was.
sm.v.head (formula)
  (medium=cylinder) Recorded at {$home}: an old woman tells the tale of the sun.
  (medium=drive) For the children of {hall.below}: the story of the sun that walked away.
  (medium=crystal) The oldest story, kept as it was told.
sm.v.end
  That is the story. Now go to sleep; the lights are going down.
  (medium=cylinder) The woman laughs at the end, and someone near the machine asks her to tell it again.
  And that is why we keep the {~hillfire} lit, even down here.
sm.s.head (formula)
  The song of the walking sun, as it was sung at {$home}.
  (medium=disc) A song on the old disc: the sun's song.
  (medium=reel) A reel from {hall.below}: the children's song of the sun.
sm.song
  {sm.s.call>.c}, {.c}, {sm.s.where}; {sm.s.we}.
sm.s.call
  come back
  walk home
  turn round
  look back
sm.s.where
  over {mountain}
  the road is long
  before the snow
  at the little fires
sm.s.we
  the fires are lit and the {herd} are waiting
  we have kept the {~hillfire} for you all night
  we will sing {~sunsong} until you hear
  they are all of us, and we are cold
sm.song.b
  The sun walked off and did not say why, and we have been singing ever since.
  The {crop} is asleep and the {herd} are thin, and the hills are bright with our fires.
  (sunway=wanderer) The wanderer has it; the wanderer is strong; sing louder, and it will let go.
  (sunway=intruder) The stranger has it, and it is happy there; sing louder, and it will remember.
  (sunway=dark) The dark has it, and the dark is deep; sing louder, and it will hear.
  (sunway=dance) Its sister has it, and they are dancing; sing louder, and it will come back to us.
sm.s.end
  The last line is sung by everyone, and the reel crackles over it.
  The song ends, and someone in the hall starts it again.
  A fire is lit in the song's last line, and the singers stop there.
sm.f.head (formula)
  The oldest story of the {people}, kept because it was right about the walking.
  (age=farfuture) A story, from before; the archive keeps it with the measurements.
  The myth of the sun, in the old words.
sm.f.reflect
  {sm.fr.a} {sm.fr.b}
sm.fr.a
  The myth says the sun walked away; it was we who walked, but the myth was made by people who stood still.
  We know now what took the sun, and the myth was not far wrong about it.
  The fires on the hills could not have been seen from where the sun was going.
  The tellers did not know what {sunway.thing} was, and they drew it anyway.
  Every child in {hall.below} knows the story before they know the stars.
  (age=farfuture) The story is the oldest thing we have that is still true of us.
sm.fr.b
  They were lit for us.
  We keep the old story anyway; it has the fires in it.
  It is kept beside the measurements, and read more often.
  The archive marks it as the first true record of the loss.
  Nobody has made a better one.

# the omens' late ages' log (genre.omens, sunlost2.vg's: kept here, a file being under 16 KB)

om.f.head (formula)
  Sky watch, {$home}: the log, cycle {#year:digits}.
  The watch's log, {$home}. Kept for the archive.
  (age=farfuture) What the watchers kept, here, before the change.
om.f.obs
  {om.fo.what}. {om.fo.tail}.
om.fo.what
  (sunway=wanderer) {sunway.thing}: nearer, as predicted
  (sunway=wanderer) {sunway.thing} crossed the inner marker [early|on time]
  (sunway=wanderer) The tracking of {sunway.thing} was handed to the second array
  (sunway=intruder) The intruder star: closer by the figure we gave last cycle
  (sunway=intruder) The intruder's light now [rivals|passes] the sun's at the solstice
  (sunway=intruder) The intruder's motion was confirmed by [three|four] stations
  (sunway=dark) The lensing round the dark mass grows; the stars there are smeared into arcs
  (sunway=dark) The dark mass is [nearer|heavier] than the last estimate
  (sunway=dark) The background stars round the dark mass were mapped again
  (sunway=dance) The companion's orbit widens again
  (sunway=dance) The companion's pull on our road was measured [again|at its height]
  (sunway=dance) The two suns' period was refitted [this cycle|after the solstice]
  (dark=1) The sun delivers less each cycle
  (dark=1) The light meters at {$home} were reset to the new noon
  (dark=1) The noon reading at {$home} fell below the old night's
om.fo.tail
  Every model agrees on what that means for our road
  There is no model in which it misses
  Our year lengthens with it, a few days each cycle
  The fields under {city} run on stored heat now
  The old figures are kept beside the new ones
  The archive has been told
  The forecast for the next cycle was not published
  The halls below were told to make ready
om.f.fields
  {om.ff.what}; {om.ff.tail}.
om.ff.what
  (harvest<=1) The yields fall again
  (harvest<=1) The surface crops failed [early|in the first frost]
  (harvest>=2) The yields held this cycle, against the trend
  (harvest>=2) The surface crops came in [thin|late], but came in
  The growers report a cold season
om.ff.tail
  the grown halls take the shortfall
  the growers are moving their plots nearer the warm ground
  the {crop} stores below are full for now
  the ration was not changed
om.f.close (formula)
  End of entry.
  The watch continues.
)VG"
